ber="299968" owner_email="wenjiaz.nvidia.com@gmail.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/68/299968/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I76f1b606c918b17753551eb76e7d6a7639b68422" commit="055c7df7b900f8ae22860674c5d38c3d1382f34c" commit_message="FROMLIST: chromiumos-overlay: revert ath10k fimrware to 10.2.4.70.12-2  Revert CL#317915.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49089 TEST=boot whirlwind and check if ath10k driver loads firmware 10.2.4.70.12-2      and associate a station and send traffic.  Change-Id: I76f1b606c918b17753551eb76e7d6a7639b68422 Signed-off-by: Zhifeng Cai &lt;caiz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320427 Commit-Ready: Yixiang Li &lt;yixiang@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yixiang Li &lt;yixiang@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320427" owner_email="yixiang@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/27/320427/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I25e7bd2f3f726b40fd4e0d9a1049a4d82bbd830d" commit="cb5dd0555c4bc3a5ff1340fc7a3038ac14cba55a" commit_message="nuc: Support rpm mode for fan control.  In order to support rpm mode, we use a TICK function (fan_tick_func) to monitor tacho value and adjust PWM duty. In this version, fan driver always enables clock source of MFT to make sure it can present real-time tacho value. For better performance, the feedback value to adjust PWM duty is various. We also change fan &amp; pwm settings for SUNUN 4-pins pwm-type fan.  Modified drivers: 1. npcx_evb/board.h: Modified fan_t &amp; pwm_t structures for SUNON fan spec. 2. npcx_evb_arm/board.h: Modified fan_t &amp; pwm_t structures for SUNON fan spec. 3. fan_chip.h: Remove unnecessary default_count field of mft_t structure 4. fan.c: Add support for rpm mode  BUG=chrome-os-partner:34346 TEST=make buildall -j; test nuvoton IC specific drivers BRANCH=none  Change-Id: I25e7bd2f3f726b40fd4e0d9a1049a4d82bbd830d Signed-off-by: Mulin Chao &lt;mlchao@nuvoton.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320510 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320510" owner_email="mlchao@nuvoton.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/10/320510/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If732f74d9e2ccc1f465f051dd6edd57093875ca4" commit="7e71866bfb34697a32427adc2cea8a3239b60b2e" commit_message="login: fix compilation of suspend handler  USE_ARC is always defined, but not always true, so we should be using #if instead of #ifdef to gate the SetUpSuspendHandler call.  BUG=chromium:574876 TEST=check logs for &quot;Registered delay&quot; message on lulu, make   sure it isn't there  Change-Id: If732f74d9e2ccc1f465f051dd6edd57093875ca4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320793 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320793" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/93/320793/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I22d259fe224cc5c13dbb7ba786cc595541fd4078" commit="8f09274485d3db842bfba11de69c767fc4f84b4e" commit_message="chell: add low battery shutdown percent  This adds the low battery shutdown percent level for chell (3%).  BUG=None TEST=on chell, open /var/log/power_manager/powerd.LATEST and check that &quot;... battery percent threshold of 3&quot; exists  Change-Id: I22d259fe224cc5c13dbb7ba786cc595541fd4078 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320465 Commit-Ready: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Derek Basehore &lt;dbasehore@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320465" owner_email="dbasehore@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/65/320465/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I1d32079b838893dce50a475d84553daf13d92b13" commit="e802dcb6e0c6911668f0c2d6fc3d46dd5c761ac4" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Add Android whitelist  Add a syscall whitelist for Android processes/apps.  BUG=b:25649436 TEST=Build and boot on veyron_minnie-cheets; download and play around with some apps.  Change-Id: I1d32079b838893dce50a475d84553daf13d92b13 Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319259 Reviewed-by: Kees Cook &lt;keescook@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319259" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/59/319259/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I96198ffb6901f0539755046ca303e94381ae7541" commit="75c6419b9bdac41ebc9ad42ef3858fadf6d69981" commit_message="wheatley: Proposed workaround for RESET_FLAG_RESET_PIN issue on wheatley.  During pressing VolUp + VolDn + Pwr buttons, Silego polls down both EC_RST_L and ROP_LDO_EN on wheatley. Beside VCC1_RST occurs, power-on reset also occurs simultaneously since EC's power rail is turned off by PMIC for a while. VCC1_RST_STS bit is cleared by power-on reset and it will influence recovery mode detection. The workaround treats no matter power-on or VCC1_RST reset as reset-pin reset. Use BOARD_WHEATLEY to distinguish them.  Modified drivers: 1. system.c: Proposed workaround for RESET_FLAG_RESET_PIN issue.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:34346 TEST=make buildall -j; test nuvoton IC specific drivers BRANCH=none  Change-Id: I96198ffb6901f0539755046ca303e94381ae7541 Signed-off-by: Mulin Chao &lt;mlchao@nuvoton.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320641 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320641" owner_email="mlchao@nuvoton.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/41/320641/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icf4ff7166ee112ee0dafd587db84bc38b34fdf40" commit="558f1f1552a930aab8dfff028575c0b7458aeb04" commit_message="quipper: test_perf_data: Attr id support; Consolidate file header classes  Add support for writing the attr id section. Previously this was always an empty section, with attrs immediately following the header. The attr ids section goes after the header, before the attrs. The perf_file_attr.ids refers to a segment of this section. Add a class (AttrIdsSection) to write the attr ids, and have it return perf_file_section structs that can be written to perf_file_attr.ids.  Because of the inserted attr ids section, the offsets for the attrs and data sections in the (normal mode) file header must now be calculate rather than using nominal values. And because of this, it is simpler to move the functionality of class ExamplePerfDataFileHeader_CustomAttrSize into ExamplePerfDataFileHeader::WithCustomAttrSize(). The updated class re-calculates the offsets of the various sections upon calling the With...() methods.  TEST=unit tests BUG=none  Change-Id: Icf4ff7166ee112ee0dafd587db84bc38b34fdf40 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320611 Commit-Ready: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320611" owner_email="dhsharp@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/11/320611/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5c3f0007b4cc8e29034bcee7075b5335c025c2b7" commit="be59176047f3f5e6e67568521aca7e8007744f13" commit_message="Credentials for remora enrollment test.  This file contains the login credentials for a test account to be used for remora testing.  BUG=None TEST=Locally  Change-Id: I5c3f0007b4cc8e29034bcee7075b5335c025c2b7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320438 Commit-Ready: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rohit Makasana &lt;rohitbm@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320438" owner_email="harpreet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/38/320438/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ieffb098e6f6a24ee8074ad97bf3be448c2917897" commit="8718584c3575769eac2fda5a62e6baf77b5d1949" commit_message="openssl: fix llvm builds (part 1 of 2).  ChromeOS with clang-built openssl fails to boot, the bug is here - https://llvm.org/bugs/show_bug.cgi?id=25527 This CL is 1 of 2 CLs to fix this bug.  This CL fixes 1 clang bug 24346.  Bug entry here - https://llvm.org/bugs/show_bug.cgi?id=24346  Notice, the patch is still under review, but I locally verified on openssl (which is the last main package that is being built by gcc), and got correct behavior. Upstream patch here - http://reviews.llvm.org/D15442  The CL to turn on clang on openssl is coming right after this CL.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:319719 BUG=See description above. TEST=build openssl using patched llvm, and got a good image. &amp;&amp; cbuildbot on daisy-release.  Change-Id: Ieffb098e6f6a24ee8074ad97bf3be448c2917897 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320302 Commit-Ready: Han Shen &lt;shenhan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Han Shen &lt;shenhan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320302" owner_email="shenhan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/02/320302/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I20620301887184c5479d694bf44682f680d6f8a3" commit="055a0209c58e6c46431bcd3d367d7e0f182aa2e7" commit_message="Reenable HW Decode test on Sandybridge.  We disabled HW Decoding on Sandybridge due to crbug/521249  BUG=None. TEST=Lab.  Change-Id: I20620301887184c5479d694bf44682f680d6f8a3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320773 Commit-Ready: Mussa Kiroga &lt;mussa@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mussa Kiroga &lt;mussa@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mussa Kiroga &lt;mussa@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320773" owner_email="mussa@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/73/320773/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7804.0.0-rc4"/></manifest>